== Description == <!--T:3--> 

<!--T:4-->
The [[Image:Sketcher_Split.svg|24px]] [[Sketcher_Split|Sketcher Split]] tool splits an edge. If the edge is a closed curve (i.e. a circle, an ellipse or a periodic B-spline) it is converted to an open curve (an arc, an elliptical arc or a non-periodic B-spline respectively).

== Usage == <!--T:6-->

<!--T:14-->
See also: [[Sketcher_Workbench#Drawing_aids|Drawing aids]].

<!--T:7-->
# There are several ways to invoke the tool:
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:Sketcher_Split.svg|16px]] [[Sketcher_Split|Split Edge]]}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Sketcher → Sketcher Tools → [[Image:Sketcher_Split.svg|16px]] Split Edge}} option from the menu.
#* Use the keyboard shortcut: {{KEY|G}} then {{KEY|Z}}.
# If there is a previous selection it is cleared. The tool does not accept a pre-selection.
# The cursor changes to a cross with the tool icon.
# Click an edge at the point where it should be split.
# If the original edge is a line or an open curve, two new edges are created connected by a [[Sketcher_ConstrainCoincident|coincident constraint]], or a point-to-point [[Sketcher_ConstrainTangent|tangent constraint]] for lines and open B-splines ({{Version|26.3}}). For closed curves a new open curve is created, the new point then does not receive a coincident constraint. Existing applicable constraints are transferred to the new edge(s). See [[#Notes|Notes]].
# This tool always runs in continue mode: optionally keep splitting edges.
# To finish, click in an empty area in the [[3D_View|3D View]], right-click or press {{KEY|Esc}}, or start another geometry or constraint creation tool.

== Notes == <!--T:10--> 

<!--T:11-->
* A [[Sketcher_ConstrainCoincident|coincident]] constraint is applied to the center points of new arcs.
* [[Sketcher_ConstrainRadius|Radius]] and [[Sketcher_ConstrainDiameter|diameter]] dimensions are transferred to one of the new arcs.
* Applicable constraints on the original start and end points are transferred to the corresponding outer endpoints of the new edges.
* A [[Sketcher_ConstrainPointOnObject|point-on-object constraint]] referring to the edge is transferred to the new edge containing the closest point to the constrained point.
* {{Version|26.3}}: [[Sketcher_ConstrainHorizontal|Horizontal]], [[Sketcher_ConstrainVertical|vertical]], [[Sketcher_ConstrainParallel|parallel]] and [[Sketcher_ConstrainAngle|angle]] constraints on a line are transferred to one new segment. The tangent constraint at the split keeps the two segments collinear.
* {{Version|26.3}}: Existing tangent and [[Sketcher_ConstrainPerpendicular|perpendicular]] constraints between edges are transferred to a new edge that intersects or is connected to the other constrained edge.
* A line's [[Sketcher_ConstrainDistance|length]], [[Sketcher_ConstrainDistanceX|horizontal length]] or [[Sketcher_ConstrainDistanceY|vertical length]] dimension becomes a dimension between the original start and end points, spanning both new segments.


